# Line endings: the repo and every working tree hold LF, whatever core.autocrlf says, so a file never ends up with
# mixed endings and a server's zip (scripts/pack.mjs) holds the same bytes as the repo. npm test checks for mixed files.
# PowerShell 5.1 and 7 both run LF scripts, and the .ps1 files have always shipped as LF, so they need no exception.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
